1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
How to make a backlight strip in Clover?

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:22,000
First, add a name line to the place where the backlight strip needs to be added.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Then modify the name line type to text.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Here you can see the name line text.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Next, make a backlight strip text in PS.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The size of the text is set to 100x200 pixels.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The resolution is 300.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
You can find some pictures with texture.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Or you can directly scan the material as a texture.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Process the interface of the texture.

11
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:24,000
After processing, let's save it.

12
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
After saving, we will add the texture of the backlight strip.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Add it to the name line texture.

14
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Then set the strength of the backlight strip.

15
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Set it to 20.

16
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Use it to create a backlight strip.

17
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Next, set the material to metal.

18
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Then adjust the roughness of the surface.

19
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Set it to 40.

20
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The strength of the backlight is 100.

21
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
The metal density is set to 80.

22
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Adjust the thickness of the name line.

23
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Set it to 5mm.

24
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Then set the thickness of the line.

25
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Set it to 1cm.

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:41,000
This is the width of the backlight strip you need.

27
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Next, I will explain how to add backlight strips to the curve.

28
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Use the free name line to add a whole circle of name lines.

29
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:58,000
You can see that if you use the name line setting just now,

30
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
the position of the backlight strip and the thickness are incompatible.

31
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
So copy a name line in the canvas window.

32
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Change this name line to the original name line.

33
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Then open the attribute editor.

34
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Then open the attribute editor.

35
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Then open the attribute editor.

36
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:28,000
In the attribute editor, adjust the gap of the name line to 1.5mm.

37
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Adjust the length of the line to 1mm.

38
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Adjust the thickness of the line to 0.30mm.

39
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Adjust the thickness of the line to 3mm.

40
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Such a position and size,

41
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
such a position and size,

42
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,860
The position and size are matching for the curve line.

43
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:54,099
But the effect now, the texture of the line has a lot of creases.

44
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:57,900
So you need to use the edit line tool.

45
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,139
Select this line.

46
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:05,060
Open the curve and smooth in the attribute editor.

47
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:09,439
You can see that the backlight strip is now smooth.

48
00:04:10,259 --> 00:04:11,500
And there are no creases.

49
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:15,960
Click to turn over, you can turn over the direction of the backlight strip.

50
00:04:17,899 --> 00:04:21,759
There is a small creases at the end of the line.

51
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:28,639
In this case, you need to add another line to cover the creases.

52
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:33,899
You also need to turn it over.

53
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:44,300
And you can see that the whole edge is smooth.

54
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,500
Now, you can add a new line to the curve.

55
00:04:48,199 --> 00:04:51,000
In this case, you need to add another line to the curve.

56
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,300
Click to turn over.

57
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,259
And there you have it.

58
00:04:56,459 --> 00:04:57,699
Now, we are going to create a new line.

59
00:04:58,199 --> 00:04:59,639
And click on the next line.

60
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,800
And we add another line to the curve.

61
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:05,800
You can see the line is now smooth.

62
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:08,699
Now, click to turn over.

63
00:05:09,399 --> 00:05:10,699
And you can see the line is smooth.

